{"task_id": "Mbpp/12", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\ndef sort_matrix(matrix: List[List[Union[int, float]]]) -> List[List[Union[int, float]]]:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a matrix by the sum of its rows in ascending order.\n    Ensures input validity and handles potential errors during sum calculation.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(matrix, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'matrix' must be a list.\")\n    \n    if not all(isinstance(row, list) for row in matrix):\n        raise TypeError(\"All elements in 'matrix' must be lists (rows).\")\n\n    rows_with_sums = []\n    for row in matrix:\n        try:\n            row_sum = sum(row)\n            rows_with_sums.append((row_sum, row))\n        except TypeError as e:\n            raise TypeError(f\"Row contains non-numeric elements: {row}\") from e\n    \n    # Python's sort is stable, preserving relative order for equal sums.\n    rows_with_sums.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n    \n    return [row for _, row in rows_with_sums]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/16", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\n# Regular expression for lowercase letters joined by underscores.\n_REGEX_LOWERCASE_UNDERSCORE = r\"^[a-z]+(_[a-z]+)+$\"\n\ndef text_lowercase_underscore(text: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates if a string contains sequences of lowercase letters joined with an underscore.\n    Raises TypeError if input is not a string.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(text, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n    return bool(re.fullmatch(_REGEX_LOWERCASE_UNDERSCORE, text))\n```"}
