{"task_id": "Mbpp/18", "solution": "```python\ndef remove_dirty_chars(source_string: str, dirty_chars: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Removes characters from source_string that are present in dirty_chars.\n    Performs case-sensitive removal and handles empty inputs gracefully.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(source_string, str) or not isinstance(dirty_chars, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Both source_string and dirty_chars must be strings.\")\n\n    if not dirty_chars:\n        return source_string\n    \n    # Use a set for efficient character lookups.\n    dirty_set = set(dirty_chars)\n    \n    result_chars = []\n    for char in source_string:\n        if char not in dirty_set:\n            result_chars.append(char)\n    \n    return \"\".join(result_chars)\n```"}
