{"task_id": "Mbpp/20", "solution": "```python\ndef is_woodall(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if the given number is a Woodall number.\n    A Woodall number is of the form n * 2^n - 1 for a natural number n >= 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(number, int) or number <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    n = 1\n    while True:\n        woodall_candidate = n * (2**n) - 1\n        if woodall_candidate == number:\n            return True\n        if woodall_candidate > number:\n            return False\n        n += 1\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/56", "solution": "```python\ndef check(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a number is one less than twice its reverse.\n    Raises TypeError if the input is not an integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(num, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'num' must be an integer.\")\n\n    def _reverse_number_local(n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Reverses the digits of an integer, preserving its sign.\"\"\"\n        if n == 0:\n            return 0\n        \n        sign = -1 if n < 0 else 1\n        abs_num_str = str(abs(n))\n        reversed_abs_num_str = abs_num_str[::-1]\n        return sign * int(reversed_abs_num_str)\n\n    reversed_num = _reverse_number_local(num)\n    return num == (2 * reversed_num) - 1\n```"}
