{"task_id": "Mbpp/56", "solution": "```python\ndef _reverse_integer(num: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Reverses the digits of an integer.\n    Handles signs and treats leading zeros as non-significant.\n    \"\"\"\n    if num == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    sign = -1 if num < 0 else 1\n    abs_num_str = str(abs(num))\n    reversed_abs_num_str = abs_num_str[::-1]\n    \n    # Converting to int naturally handles leading zeros (e.g., \"07\" becomes 7).\n    return sign * int(reversed_abs_num_str)\n\ndef check(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a number is one less than twice its reverse.\n    Raises TypeError if input is not an integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(num, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be an integer.\")\n\n    reversed_num = _reverse_integer(num)\n    target_value = (2 * reversed_num) - 1\n    \n    return num == target_value\n```"}
