{"task_id": "Mbpp/57", "solution": "```python\nfrom functools import cmp_to_key\nfrom typing import List\n\nclass InvalidDigitError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid digit inputs.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n\ndef find_Max_Num(digits: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Constructs the largest number from a list of digits.\n    It validates inputs, sorts digits using a custom comparison, and handles edge cases.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Validate that all elements are integers between 0 and 9.\n    if not isinstance(digits, list):\n        raise InvalidDigitError(\"Input must be a list of integers.\")\n    for digit in digits:\n        if not isinstance(digit, int):\n            raise InvalidDigitError(f\"Invalid digit type: {type(digit)}. Expected int.\")\n        if not (0 <= digit <= 9):\n            raise InvalidDigitError(f\"Digit out of range: {digit}. Expected 0-9.\")\n\n    if not digits:\n        return 0\n\n    digit_strings = [str(d) for d in digits]\n\n    # Define the custom comparison logic as per specification.\n    def _compare(a: str, b: str) -> int:\n        if (a + b) > (b + a):\n            return -1  # a should come before b\n        elif (a + b) < (b + a):\n            return 1   # b should come before a\n        else:\n            return 0\n\n    # Sort the string representations of digits using the custom comparison.\n    digit_strings.sort(key=cmp_to_key(_compare))\n\n    # If the largest number starts with '0' (e.g., [0, 0, 0]), the result is 0.\n    if digit_strings and digit_strings[0] == '0':\n        return 0\n\n    largest_num_str = \"\".join(digit_strings)\n    return int(largest_num_str)\n```"}
