{"task_id": "Mbpp/68", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\ndef is_Monotonic(arr: List[Union[int, float]]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an array is monotonic (either non-increasing or non-decreasing).\n    An empty or single-element array is always considered monotonic.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(arr) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    def _is_non_increasing(local_arr: List[Union[int, float]]) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Helper to check if the array is non-increasing.\"\"\"\n        for i in range(len(local_arr) - 1):\n            if local_arr[i] < local_arr[i+1]:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    def _is_non_decreasing(local_arr: List[Union[int, float]]) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Helper to check if the array is non-decreasing.\"\"\"\n        for i in range(len(local_arr) - 1):\n            if local_arr[i] > local_arr[i+1]:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    return _is_non_increasing(arr) or _is_non_decreasing(arr)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/69", "solution": "```python\ndef is_sublist(main_list: list, sub_list: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if sub_list is present as a contiguous sequence within main_list.\n    Returns True if found, False otherwise, adhering to specific sublist rules.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not sub_list:\n        return True\n    if len(sub_list) > len(main_list):\n        return False\n    \n    n = len(main_list)\n    m = len(sub_list)\n    \n    for i in range(n - m + 1):\n        if main_list[i : i + m] == sub_list:\n            return True\n    return False\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/69", "solution": "```python\ndef is_sublist(main_list: list, sub_list: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given sublist is a contiguous sublist of the main list.\n\n    Args:\n        main_list: The list to search within.\n        sub_list: The list to search for.\n\n    Returns:\n        True if sub_list is found contiguously within main_list, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not sub_list:\n        return True  # An empty list is always a sublist\n\n    if not main_list or len(sub_list) > len(main_list):\n        return False\n\n    n = len(main_list)\n    m = len(sub_list)\n\n    for i in range(n - m + 1):\n        if main_list[i : i + m] == sub_list:\n            return True\n    return False\n```"}
