{"task_id": "Mbpp/75", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Tuple\n\ndef find_tuples(list_of_tuples: List[Tuple[int, ...]], k: int) -> List[Tuple[int, ...]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Filters a list of tuples, returning only those where every element is divisible by k.\n    Raises ValueError for k=0 or TypeError for incorrect input element types.\n    \"\"\"\n    if k == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Divisor 'k' cannot be zero.\")\n\n    filtered_tuples: List[Tuple[int, ...]] = []\n\n    for current_tuple in list_of_tuples:\n        if not isinstance(current_tuple, tuple):\n            raise TypeError(f\"Expected a tuple, but got {type(current_tuple).__name__} in the list.\")\n\n        all_elements_divisible = True\n        for element in current_tuple:\n            if not isinstance(element, int):\n                raise TypeError(f\"Expected an integer in tuple, but got {type(element).__name__}.\")\n            if element % k != 0:\n                all_elements_divisible = False\n                break\n        \n        if all_elements_divisible:\n            filtered_tuples.append(current_tuple)\n    \n    return filtered_tuples\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/77", "solution": "```python\ndef is_Diff(number):\n    \"\"\"Checks if an integer is divisible by 11 using the alternating sum of digits rule.\n    Raises ValueError if input is not an integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(number, int):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be an integer.\")\n\n    if number == 0:\n        return True\n\n    s_number = str(abs(number))\n    alternating_sum = 0\n\n    for i, digit_char in enumerate(s_number):\n        digit = int(digit_char)\n        if i % 2 == 0:\n            alternating_sum += digit\n        else:\n            alternating_sum -= digit\n\n    return alternating_sum % 11 == 0\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/80", "solution": "```python\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input values.\n    This is raised when 'n' does not meet the non-negative integer requirement.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\ndef tetrahedral_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth tetrahedral number using the formula T_n = n * (n + 1) * (n + 2) / 6.\n    The input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"n must be an integer.\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"n must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    # Using integer division since tetrahedral numbers are always integers.\n    return (n * (n + 1) * (n + 2)) // 6\n```"}
