{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "```python\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input to the Newman-Conway sequence function.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\ndef sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth number of the Newman-Conway sequence using memoization.\n    Raises InvalidInputError if n is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    # Initialize memoization dictionary as a function attribute for persistence.\n    # This stores previously computed values to avoid redundant calculations.\n    if not hasattr(sequence, '_memo'):\n        sequence._memo = {1: 1, 2: 1}\n\n    if n in sequence._memo:\n        return sequence._memo[n]\n\n    # Apply the Newman-Conway recurrence relation: P(n) = P(P(n - 1)) + P(n - P(n - 1)).\n    p_n_minus_1 = sequence(n - 1)\n    term1 = sequence(p_n_minus_1)\n    term2 = sequence(n - p_n_minus_1)\n\n    result = term1 + term2\n    sequence._memo[n] = result\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/85", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef surfacearea_sphere(radius: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the surface area of a sphere given its radius.\n    Raises ValueError if the radius is not a non-negative number.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(radius, (int, float)):\n        raise ValueError(\"Radius must be a numeric value.\")\n    if radius < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Radius cannot be negative.\")\n\n    return 4 * math.pi * (radius ** 2)\n```"}
