{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "```python\n# The memoization cache is kept at the module level to persist across calls\n# and satisfy the \"no class wrapper\" and \"bare function\" requirements,\n# while still providing the specified memoization behavior.\n_memo = {1: 1, 2: 1}\n\ndef sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the nth Newman-Conway number using memoization.\n    Raises ValueError if n is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    # Calculate P(n) using the recursive definition: P(P(n - 1)) + P(n - P(n - 1)).\n    # Recursive calls will utilize the same module-level _memo for efficiency.\n    p_n_minus_1_val = sequence(n - 1)\n    p_p_n_minus_1_val = sequence(p_n_minus_1_val)\n    p_n_minus_p_n_minus_1_val = sequence(n - p_n_minus_1_val)\n\n    result = p_p_n_minus_1_val + p_n_minus_p_n_minus_1_val\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result\n```"}
