{"task_id": "Mbpp/93", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Union\n\ndef power(a: Union[int, float], b: int) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"Calculates 'a' raised to the power of 'b' using an iterative approach.\n    Handles zero, positive, and negative integer exponents, raising errors for invalid types or operations.\"\"\"\n\n    if not isinstance(a, (int, float)):\n        raise TypeError(\"Base 'a' must be an integer or a float.\")\n    if not isinstance(b, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Exponent 'b' must be an integer.\")\n\n    if b == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    if b > 0:\n        result = 1\n        for _ in range(b):\n            result *= a\n        return result\n    else:  # b < 0\n        if a == 0:\n            raise ZeroDivisionError(\"Cannot raise 0 to a negative power.\")\n        \n        positive_power_result = power(a, -b)\n        return 1 / positive_power_result\n```\n"}
