{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the Eulerian number a(n, m) using its standard formula.\n    Raises TypeError for non-integer inputs or ValueError for negative inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or not isinstance(m, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Inputs n and m must be integers.\")\n    if n < 0 or m < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Inputs n and m must be non-negative.\")\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1 if m == 0 else 0\n\n    def _nCk(N: int, K: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the binomial coefficient \\\"N choose K\\\". Returns 0 if K is out of range.\"\"\"\n        if K < 0 or K > N:\n            return 0\n        return math.factorial(N) // (math.factorial(K) * math.factorial(N - K))\n\n    result = 0\n    for k in range(m + 1):\n        term = ((-1)**k) * _nCk(n + 1, k) * ((m + 1 - k)**n)\n        result += term\n    return result\n```"}
