{"task_id": "Mbpp/98", "solution": "```python\ndef multiply_num(numbers: list[float | int]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Multiplies all numbers in a list and divides the product by the list's length.\n    Returns 0.0 if the list is empty, and raises TypeError for non-numeric elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        return 0.0\n\n    product = 1.0\n    for number in numbers:\n        if not isinstance(number, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements in the list must be numbers (int or float).\")\n        product *= number\n\n    return product / len(numbers)\n```"}
