{"task_id": "Mbpp/125", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input to binary analysis functions.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\ndef find_length(binary_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum difference between the count of 0s and 1s in any substring of a binary string.\n    Uses Kadane's algorithm after transforming '0's to 1 and '1's to -1.\n    \"\"\"\n    # FR1: Validate input type.\n    if not isinstance(binary_string, str):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n    \n    # FR4: Handle empty input strings.\n    if not binary_string:\n        return 0\n\n    # FR1 & BR1: Validate input string content using regex.\n    if not re.fullmatch(\"[01]+\", binary_string):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input string must contain only '0' or '1'.\")\n\n    # FR2: Transform '0' to 1 and '1' to -1 for Kadane's algorithm.\n    transformed_array = [1 if char == '0' else -1 for char in binary_string]\n    \n    # Apply Kadane's algorithm to find the maximum subarray sum.\n    # This sum represents the maximum difference (count of 0s - count of 1s).\n    max_so_far = transformed_array[0]\n    current_max = transformed_array[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(transformed_array)):\n        current_max = max(transformed_array[i], current_max + transformed_array[i])\n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n        \n    # FR3: Return the integer result.\n    return max_so_far\n```"}
