{"task_id": "Mbpp/126", "solution": "```python\nimport builtins\n\ndef _is_positive_integer(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a value is a positive integer.\"\"\"\n    return isinstance(num, int) and num > 0\n\ndef _get_divisors(num: int) -> set[int]:\n    \"\"\"Returns a set of all positive divisors for a positive integer.\n    This helper performs its own validation for robustness.\"\"\"\n    if not _is_positive_integer(num):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a positive integer.\")\n    \n    divs = set()\n    for i in range(1, int(num**0.5) + 1):\n        if num % i == 0:\n            divs.add(i)\n            divs.add(num // i)\n    return divs\n\ndef sum(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of common divisors for two positive integers.\"\"\"\n    # Validate both inputs as positive integers (FR1, BR1).\n    if not (_is_positive_integer(num1) and _is_positive_integer(num2)):\n        raise ValueError(\"Both inputs must be positive integers.\")\n    \n    # Identify all common divisors (FR2).\n    divisors1 = _get_divisors(num1)\n    divisors2 = _get_divisors(num2)\n    common_divs = divisors1.intersection(divisors2)\n    \n    # Sum the identified common divisors (FR3, FR4).\n    return builtins.sum(common_divs)\n```"}
