{"task_id": "Mbpp/131", "solution": "```python\ndef reverse_vowels(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Reverses only the vowels in a given string, preserving other characters.\n    'y' is not considered a vowel.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_string, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n\n    # Define vowels set and helper function locally to keep it self-contained.\n    _VOWELS_SET = {'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'}\n    def _is_vowel(char: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a character is a vowel (case-insensitive).\"\"\"\n        return char.lower() in _VOWELS_SET\n\n    chars = list(input_string)\n    vowel_indices = []\n    vowels = []\n\n    # First pass: identify vowels and their positions.\n    for i, char in enumerate(chars):\n        if _is_vowel(char):\n            vowel_indices.append(i)\n            vowels.append(char)\n\n    # Reverse the collected vowels.\n    vowels.reverse()\n\n    # Second pass: place reversed vowels back into original positions.\n    for i, vowel_char in zip(vowel_indices, vowels):\n        chars[i] = vowel_char\n\n    return \"\".join(chars)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/132", "solution": "```python\ndef tup_string(input_tuple: tuple) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Converts a tuple of elements into a single concatenated string.\n    Raises TypeError if input is not a tuple or elements are not string-convertible.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_tuple, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a tuple.\")\n    try:\n        return \"\".join(input_tuple)\n    except TypeError as e:\n        raise TypeError(f\"Tuple elements must be string-convertible: {e}\") from e\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/131", "solution": "```python\ndef reverse_vowels(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Reverses only the vowels of a given string, treating 'y' as a consonant.\n    Preserves original case and character positions for non-vowels.\n    \"\"\"\n    VOWELS_SET = {'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'}\n\n    def _is_vowel(char: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a character is a vowel (case-insensitive).\"\"\"\n        return char.lower() in VOWELS_SET\n\n    vowels_in_string = []\n    # Collect all vowels from the input string in their original order.\n    for char in s:\n        if _is_vowel(char):\n            vowels_in_string.append(char)\n\n    # Reverse the collected vowels.\n    reversed_vowels = vowels_in_string[::-1]\n\n    result_chars = []\n    reversed_vowel_idx = 0\n    # Construct the new string by replacing original vowels with reversed ones.\n    for char in s:\n        if _is_vowel(char):\n            result_chars.append(reversed_vowels[reversed_vowel_idx])\n            reversed_vowel_idx += 1\n        else:\n            result_chars.append(char)\n\n    return \"\".join(result_chars)\n```"}
