{"task_id": "Mbpp/133", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_negativenum(numbers: list[float | int]) -> float | int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all negative numbers in a given list.\n    Handles type checking and returns 0 for empty lists or no negative numbers.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(numbers, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    has_float = False\n\n    for num in numbers:\n        if not isinstance(num, (int, float)):\n            raise ValueError(f\"List element '{num}' is not a number.\")\n        if isinstance(num, float):\n            has_float = True\n        if num < 0:\n            total_sum += num\n\n    return float(total_sum) if has_float else int(total_sum)\n```"}
