{"task_id": "Mbpp/166", "solution": "```python\ndef find_even_pair(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts pairs of integers in a list that XOR to an even number.\n    This occurs when both numbers in a pair have the same parity (both even or both odd).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(numbers, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n\n    count_odd = 0\n    count_even = 0\n\n    for num in numbers:\n        if not isinstance(num, int):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements in the list must be integers.\")\n        if num % 2 == 0:\n            count_even += 1\n        else:\n            count_odd += 1\n\n    # Calculate pairs using the combination formula n * (n - 1) / 2.\n    odd_odd_pairs = (count_odd * (count_odd - 1)) // 2\n    even_even_pairs = (count_even * (count_even - 1)) // 2\n\n    return odd_odd_pairs + even_even_pairs\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/170", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\ndef sum_range_list(numbers: List[Union[int, float]], start_index: int, end_index: int) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of numbers in a list within a specified inclusive range.\n    Handles various input validation and raises appropriate exceptions.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(numbers, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'numbers' must be a list.\")\n    if not isinstance(start_index, int) or not isinstance(end_index, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"start_index and end_index must be integers.\")\n\n    if start_index > end_index:\n        raise ValueError(\"start_index cannot be greater than end_index.\")\n    if not numbers: # Handles cases where numbers is an empty list\n        raise IndexError(\"Cannot sum range on an empty list.\")\n    if not (0 <= start_index < len(numbers) and 0 <= end_index < len(numbers)):\n        raise IndexError(\"start_index or end_index is out of bounds for the list.\")\n\n    current_sum: Union[int, float] = 0\n    for i in range(start_index, end_index + 1):\n        if not isinstance(numbers[i], (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(f\"Element at index {i} is not a number: {numbers[i]}\")\n        current_sum += numbers[i]\n    return current_sum\n```"}
