{"task_id": "Mbpp/167", "solution": "```python\ndef next_power_of_2(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the smallest power of 2 greater than or equal to n.\n    Handles type and value validation, returning 1 for n=0 and raising errors for invalid inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(f\"Parameter 'n' must be an integer, but got {type(n).__name__}.\")\n\n    # For n < 0, raise ValueError as per functional requirements.\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Parameter 'n' must be non-negative, but got {n}.\")\n    \n    # For n=0 or n=1, the smallest power of 2 greater than or equal to n is 1.\n    if n <= 1:\n        return 1\n    \n    # If n is already a power of 2, return n. This check is valid for n > 0.\n    if (n & (n - 1)) == 0:\n        return n\n\n    # Calculate the smallest power of 2 greater than n using bit manipulation.\n    # This algorithm efficiently finds the next power of 2 by setting all bits below the MSB, then adding 1.\n    n -= 1\n    n |= n >> 1\n    n |= n >> 2\n    n |= n >> 4\n    n |= n >> 8\n    n |= n >> 16\n    n |= n >> 32 \n    return n + 1\n```"}
