{"task_id": "Mbpp/172", "solution": "```python\nSUBSTRING_TO_COUNT: str = \"std\"\n\ndef count_occurance(input_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts non-overlapping, case-sensitive occurrences of 'std' in the input string.\n    Raises TypeError if the input is not a string.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_string, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n\n    count = 0\n    start_index = 0\n    while True:\n        index = input_string.find(SUBSTRING_TO_COUNT, start_index)\n        if index == -1:\n            break\n        count += 1\n        start_index = index + len(SUBSTRING_TO_COUNT)\n    return count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/170", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\ndef sum_range_list(number_list: List[Union[int, float]], start_index: int, end_index: int) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of numbers in a list within a specified range (inclusive).\n    This function performs robust validation on the input list and indices.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Validate number_list\n    if not isinstance(number_list, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'number_list' must be a list.\")\n    if not number_list:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'number_list' cannot be empty.\")\n    for item in number_list:\n        if not isinstance(item, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements in 'number_list' must be numbers (int or float).\")\n\n    # Validate indices\n    if not isinstance(start_index, int) or not isinstance(end_index, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Indices must be integers.\")\n    \n    list_length = len(number_list)\n    if start_index < 0 or end_index < 0:\n        raise IndexError(\"Indices cannot be negative.\")\n    if start_index >= list_length or end_index >= list_length:\n        raise IndexError(\"Indices are out of bounds for the given list length.\")\n    if start_index > end_index:\n        raise ValueError(\"start_index cannot be greater than end_index.\")\n\n    # Calculate sum\n    current_sum: Union[int, float] = 0\n    for i in range(start_index, end_index + 1):\n        current_sum += number_list[i]\n    return current_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/222", "solution": "```python\ndef check_type(data_tuple: tuple) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if all elements in the tuple have the same data type.\n    Raises TypeError if input is not a tuple.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(data_tuple, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a tuple.\")\n\n    if not data_tuple or len(data_tuple) == 1:\n        return True\n\n    first_element_type = type(data_tuple[0])\n    for element in data_tuple[1:]:\n        if type(element) is not first_element_type:\n            return False\n    return True\n```"}
