{"task_id": "Mbpp/224", "solution": "```python\ndef count_Set_Bits(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of set bits (binary digits with value 1) in a given integer.\n    Handles negative numbers by taking their absolute value.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Ensure the input is an integer.\n    if not isinstance(number, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'number' must be an integer.\")\n\n    # Handle negative numbers by taking their absolute value as per FR5 in the design.\n    # This is a common interpretation when two's complement for negative numbers\n    # is not explicitly requested for bit counting.\n    abs_number = abs(number)\n\n    # Convert the absolute number to its binary representation and count the '1's.\n    # The `bin()` function returns a string prefixed with \"0b\", e.g., \"0b101\".\n    # `count('1')` then efficiently counts the occurrences of '1' in this string.\n    return bin(abs_number).count('1')\n\n```"}
