{"task_id": "Mbpp/232", "solution": "import heapq\n\ndef larg_nnum(data_list: list, n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies and returns a list containing the n largest items from data_list.\n    This function leverages heapq.nlargest for efficient retrieval.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        return []\n    \n    # If n is greater than or equal to the list length, return a copy of the entire list.\n    if n >= len(data_list):\n        return list(data_list)\n    \n    return heapq.nlargest(n, data_list)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/232", "solution": "```python\ndef larg_nnum(input_list: list, n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns a new list containing the n largest items from the input list, sorted in descending order.\n    Handles type validation, non-positive n, and n larger than list length gracefully.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_list, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"input_list must be a list.\")\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"n must be an integer.\")\n\n    if n <= 0:\n        return []\n\n    sorted_list = sorted(input_list, reverse=True)\n    return sorted_list[:n]\n```"}
