{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Any, Dict\n\ndef check_occurences(list_of_tuples: List[Tuple[Any, ...]]) -> Dict[Tuple[Any, ...], int]:\n    \"\"\"Counts occurrences of canonical tuple representations in a list.\n    Tuples are canonicalized by sorting their elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    occurrence_map: Dict[Tuple[Any, ...], int] = {}\n    for tup in list_of_tuples:\n        # Canonicalize the tuple by sorting its elements and converting back to a tuple.\n        canonical_tup = tuple(sorted(tup))\n        occurrence_map[canonical_tup] = occurrence_map.get(canonical_tup, 0) + 1\n    return occurrence_map\n```"}
