{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "```python\ndef even_bit_set_number(num: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets all even-indexed bits (0, 2, 4, ...) of a given number to 1,\n    up to the most significant bit of the input number. Raises ValueError if the input number is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if num < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input number must be non-negative for this operation.\")\n    if num == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    result = num\n    max_bit_pos = num.bit_length() - 1\n\n    for i in range(max_bit_pos + 1):\n        if i % 2 == 0:  # If it's an even-indexed bit position\n            result |= (1 << i) # Set the bit at position i\n\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "```python\nimport functools\n\ndef get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of possible sequences of length n.\n    Each element x_i must be a positive integer, x_i >= 2 * x_{i-1}, and x_i <= m.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(m, int) or m <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"m must be a positive integer.\")\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    @functools.lru_cache(None)\n    def _count_recursive(current_element: int, remaining_length: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Counts sequences recursively, using memoization for efficiency.\"\"\"\n        if remaining_length == 0:\n            return 1  # A valid sequence of length n has been formed.\n\n        count = 0\n        min_next_element = 2 * current_element\n        for next_element in range(min_next_element, m + 1):\n            count += _count_recursive(next_element, remaining_length - 1)\n        return count\n\n    total_sequences = 0\n    for start_element in range(1, m + 1):\n        total_sequences += _count_recursive(start_element, n - 1)\n\n    return total_sequences\n```"}
