{"task_id": "Mbpp/244", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef next_Perfect_Square(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the smallest perfect square strictly greater than the input number.\n    Raises ValueError for non-integer or negative inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(number, int):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be an integer.\")\n    if number < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    if number == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Find the integer square root of the number.\n    current_root = math.isqrt(number)\n\n    # The next perfect square is the square of (current_root + 1).\n    next_root = current_root + 1\n    \n    return next_root * next_root\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/244", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input to perfect square calculations.\n    Inherits from ValueError for consistent error handling.\n    \"\"\"\n    pass\n\ndef next_Perfect_Square(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the smallest perfect square strictly greater than a given integer `n`.\n    Handles non-integer or negative inputs by raising `InvalidInputError`.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Invalid input: n must be an integer.\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Invalid input: n must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    # Find the integer part of the square root of n.\n    # For example, for n=35, math.isqrt(35) is 5. For n=25, math.isqrt(25) is 5.\n    sqrt_n_int = math.isqrt(n)\n\n    # The next integer whose square will be strictly greater than n.\n    # If n=25, sqrt_n_int is 5, next_root will be 6, and 6*6=36.\n    # If n=35, sqrt_n_int is 5, next_root will be 6, and 6*6=36.\n    next_root = sqrt_n_int + 1\n    return next_root * next_root\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "```python\ndef lps(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the length of the longest palindromic subsequence of the input string s.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n\n    n = len(s)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the LPS for substring s[i...j].\n    dp = [[0 for _ in range(n)] for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # Every single character is a palindrome of length 1.\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the dp table by iterating through substring lengths.\n    for L in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - L + 1):\n            j = i + L - 1\n            if s[i] == s[j] and L == 2:\n                dp[i][j] = 2\n            elif s[i] == s[j]:\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i + 1][j - 1]\n            else:\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i][j - 1], dp[i + 1][j])\n\n    return dp[0][n - 1]\n```"}
