{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "```python\ndef lps(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the length of the longest palindromic subsequence of a string.\n    Uses dynamic programming with O(n^2) time and space complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n\n    n = len(s)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the longest palindromic subsequence of s[i..j].\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # Single characters are palindromes of length 1.\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table for substrings of increasing length.\n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            j = i + length - 1\n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                # If end characters match, add 2 to LPS of inner substring.\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + (dp[i + 1][j - 1] if length > 2 else 0)\n            else:\n                # If they don't match, take max of excluding s[i] or s[j].\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n\n    return dp[0][n - 1]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "```python\nclass BitonicSubsequenceException(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for errors in bitonic subsequence operations.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\ndef _validate_array_of_integers(arr: list) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Validates if the input is a list of integers.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(arr, list):\n        raise BitonicSubsequenceException(\"Input must be a list.\")\n    for item in arr:\n        if not isinstance(item, int):\n            raise BitonicSubsequenceException(\"All elements in the list must be integers.\")\n\ndef _calculate_lis_sums(arr: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at each position.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    lis_sums = list(arr)\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j] and lis_sums[i] < lis_sums[j] + arr[i]:\n                lis_sums[i] = lis_sums[j] + arr[i]\n    return lis_sums\n\ndef _calculate_lds_sums(arr: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum sum of a decreasing subsequence starting at each position.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    lds_sums = list(arr)\n    for i in range(n - 2, -1, -1):\n        for j in range(n - 1, i, -1):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j] and lds_sums[i] < lds_sums[j] + arr[i]:\n                lds_sums[i] = lds_sums[j] + arr[i]\n    return lds_sums\n\ndef max_sum(array: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence within the given array.\n    A bitonic subsequence is first strictly increasing and then strictly decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_array_of_integers(array)\n\n    n = len(array)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return array[0]\n\n    # Initialize max_bitonic_sum_val with the maximum element\n    # as any single element is a valid bitonic subsequence.\n    max_bitonic_sum_val = max(array)\n\n    lis_sums = _calculate_lis_sums(array)\n    lds_sums = _calculate_lds_sums(array)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        # Combine LIS and LDS sums at peak 'i'. Subtract array[i] as it's counted twice.\n        current_bitonic_sum = lis_sums[i] + lds_sums[i] - array[i]\n        max_bitonic_sum_val = max(max_bitonic_sum_val, current_bitonic_sum)\n\n    return max_bitonic_sum_val\n```"}
