{"task_id": "Mbpp/252", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef convert(z_input):\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a complex number to its polar coordinate representation (magnitude, phase).\n    Handles int, float, or complex inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    if isinstance(z_input, (int, float)):\n        real_part = float(z_input)\n        imag_part = 0.0\n    elif isinstance(z_input, complex):\n        real_part = z_input.real\n        imag_part = z_input.imag\n    else:\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a numeric type (int, float, or complex).\")\n\n    magnitude = math.sqrt(real_part**2 + imag_part**2)\n    phase = math.atan2(imag_part, real_part)\n\n    return (magnitude, phase)\n```"}
