{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "```python\ndef _is_prime(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a number is prime using trial division.\n    It returns True for prime numbers, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 2:\n        return False\n    for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return False\n    return True\n\ndef count_Primes_nums(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts prime numbers strictly less than the given number.\n    Raises ValueError for non-integer or negative inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(number, int) or number < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    if number <= 2:\n        return 0\n\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(2, number):\n        if _is_prime(i):\n            count += 1\n            \n    return count\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "```python\ndef count_Primes_nums(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts prime numbers strictly less than the given non-negative integer.\n    Raises ValueError if the input is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a number is prime. Returns True for primes, False otherwise.\"\"\"\n        if num < 2:\n            return False\n        for i in range(2, int(num**0.5) + 1):\n            if num % i == 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    if number < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'number' must be a non-negative number.\")\n\n    count = 0\n    for num in range(number):\n        if _is_prime(num):\n            count += 1\n    return count\n```"}
