{"task_id": "Mbpp/277", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Union\n\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input arguments.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\ndef dict_filter(data_dict: Dict[Any, Union[int, float]], n: int) -> Dict[Any, Union[int, float]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Filters a dictionary, retaining key-value pairs where the value is greater than or equal to n.\n    Raises InvalidInputError for incorrect input types.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(data_dict, dict):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"data_dict must be a dictionary.\")\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"n must be an integer.\")\n\n    filtered_dict = {key: value for key, value in data_dict.items() if value >= n}\n    return filtered_dict\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/277", "solution": "```python\ndef dict_filter(input_dict: dict, n: int) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Filters a dictionary to include only entries where the value is an integer\n    greater than or equal to n.\n\n    Raises TypeError if input_dict is not a dictionary or n is not an integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_dict, dict):\n        raise TypeError(\"input_dict must be a dictionary\")\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"n must be an integer\")\n\n    filtered_dict = {}\n    for key, value in input_dict.items():\n        if isinstance(value, int) and value >= n:\n            filtered_dict[key] = value\n    return filtered_dict\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/279", "solution": "```python\ndef is_num_decagonal(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth decagonal number.\n    Raises ValueError if n is not a positive integer.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise ValueError(f\"Parameter 'n' must be an integer, but received type {type(n).__name__}.\")\n    if n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Parameter 'n' must be a positive integer, but received {n}.\")\n\n    return n * (4 * n - 3)\n```"}
