{"task_id": "Mbpp/282", "solution": "```python\nclass ListOperationError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for errors during list operations.\n    Provides a descriptive error message for invalid operations.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\ndef sub_list(list1: list[int | float], list2: list[int | float]) -> list[int | float]:\n    \"\"\"Subtracts two lists element-wise, returning a new list with the results.\n    Raises ListOperationError for invalid input lengths or non-numeric elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not list1 or not list2:\n        raise ListOperationError(\"Input lists cannot be empty.\")\n    if len(list1) != len(list2):\n        raise ListOperationError(\"Lists must have the same length for element-wise subtraction.\")\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(list1)):\n        try:\n            diff = list1[i] - list2[i]\n            result.append(diff)\n        except TypeError:\n            raise ListOperationError(\"List elements must be numeric (int or float).\")\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "```python\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef validate(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the frequency of each digit in the integer is less than or equal to the digit itself.\n    Raises TypeError if the input 'number' is not an integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(number, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'number' must be an integer.\")\n\n    if number < 0:\n        number = abs(number)\n\n    if number == 0:\n        return False\n\n    num_str = str(number)\n    digit_counts = Counter(num_str)\n\n    for digit_char, count in digit_counts.items():\n        digit_value = int(digit_char)\n        if count > digit_value:\n            return False\n    return True\n```"}
