{"task_id": "Mbpp/260", "solution": "To find the nth Newman\u2013Shanks\u2013Williams prime number, define the function `newman_prime(n)`.\n\n```python\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"\n    Custom exception for invalid input parameters.\n    It indicates that provided input did not meet the required criteria.\n    \"\"\"\n    pass\n\nclass InputValidator:\n    @staticmethod\n    def validate_n(n: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Validates that 'n' is a non-negative integer.\n        It raises InvalidInputError if 'n' is not an integer or is negative.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(n, int):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n        if n < 0:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\nclass NSWCalculator:\n    @staticmethod\n    def calculate_nsw_number(index: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the NSW number at a given index.\n        It uses the recurrence relation S_n = 2 * S_{n-1} + S_{n-2}.\n        \"\"\"\n        if index == 0:\n            return 1\n        elif index == 1:\n            return 1\n        \n        s_prev2 = 1 # S_0\n        s_prev1 = 1 # S_1\n        for _ in range(2, index + 1):\n            s_current = 2 * s_prev1 + s_prev2\n            s_prev2 = s_prev1\n            s_prev1 = s_current\n        return s_prev1\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Determines if a given number is prime.\n        It considers 1 as a prime for consistency with NSW prime sequence definition.\n        \"\"\"\n        if num == 1: # Special case for NSW prime sequence\n            return True\n        if num < 2:\n            return False\n        for i in range(2, int(num**0.5) + 1):\n            if num % i == 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def find_nth_nsw_prime(n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Iteratively finds the nth Newman-Shanks-Williams prime number.\n        It raises ValueError if n is 0 as there's no 0th prime in a 1-indexed sequence.\n        \"\"\"\n        if n == 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"There is no 0th NSW prime number in a 1-indexed sequence.\")\n        \n        nsw_primes_found = 0\n        current_nsw_index = 0\n        while True:\n            nsw_num = NSWCalculator.calculate_nsw_number(current_nsw_index)\n            if NSWCalculator.is_prime(nsw_num):\n                nsw_primes_found += 1\n                if nsw_primes_found == n:\n                    return nsw_num\n            current_nsw_index += 1\n\ndef newman_prime(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the nth Newman-Shanks-Williams prime number.\n    It raises InvalidInputError for invalid 'n' or ValueError if 'n' is 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    InputValidator.validate_n(n)\n    return NSWCalculator.find_nth_nsw_prime(n)\n```\n"}
