{"task_id": "Mbpp/301", "solution": "```python\ndef dict_depth(d: dict) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum nesting depth of a dictionary.\n    The outermost dictionary is depth 1; each nested dictionary adds 1 to the depth.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(d, dict):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a dictionary.\")\n\n    max_current_depth = 0\n    for value in d.values():\n        if isinstance(value, dict):\n            max_current_depth = max(max_current_depth, dict_depth(value))\n    \n    return 1 + max_current_depth\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/305", "solution": "```python\ndef start_withp(word_list: list[str]) -> tuple[str, ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts up to two words from a list of strings that start with 'p' (case-insensitive).\n    Raises TypeError if input is not a list or contains non-string elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    TARGET_START_LETTER = \"p\"\n    MAX_WORDS_TO_EXTRACT = 2\n\n    if not isinstance(word_list, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'word_list' must be a list.\")\n\n    found_words = []\n    for item in word_list:\n        if not isinstance(item, str):\n            raise TypeError(f\"All elements in 'word_list' must be strings, but found type {type(item).__name__}.\")\n            \n        words_in_item = item.split()\n        for word in words_in_item:\n            if word.lower().startswith(TARGET_START_LETTER):\n                found_words.append(word)\n                if len(found_words) == MAX_WORDS_TO_EXTRACT:\n                    return tuple(found_words)\n    return tuple(found_words)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/305", "solution": "```python\ndef start_withp(word_list: list[str]) -> tuple[str | None, str | None]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts the first two words starting with 'p' (case-insensitive) from a list of text phrases.\n    Returns a tuple of two words, using None for missing elements if fewer than two are found.\n    \"\"\"\n    found_words = []\n    for phrase in word_list:\n        words_in_phrase = phrase.split()\n        for word in words_in_phrase:\n            if word and word[0].lower() == 'p':\n                found_words.append(word)\n                if len(found_words) == 2:\n                    return (found_words[0], found_words[1])\n    \n    if len(found_words) == 1:\n        return (found_words[0], None)\n    else:\n        return (None, None)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/308", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\ndef large_product(list1: List[Union[int, float]], list2: List[Union[int, float]], k: int) -> List[Union[int, float]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the k largest products from elements of two lists.\n    The products are returned in descending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not list1 or not list2:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input lists cannot be empty.\")\n    if not isinstance(k, int) or k <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"k must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    all_products = [x * y for x in list1 for y in list2]\n    all_products.sort(reverse=True)\n    return all_products[:k]\n```"}
