{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "```python\ndef set_left_most_unset_bit(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets the leftmost unset bit in a non-negative integer.\n    If all current bits are set, the next higher bit is set.\"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        return n\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    msb_pos = n.bit_length() - 1\n\n    for i in range(msb_pos, -1, -1):\n        if not (n & (1 << i)):\n            return n | (1 << i)\n\n    return n | (1 << (msb_pos + 1))\n```"}
