{"task_id": "Mbpp/388", "solution": "```python\ndef highest_Power_of_2(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the highest power of 2 that is less than or equal to n.\n    Raises ValueError if n is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    power = 1\n    # Repeatedly left-shift 'power' until it exceeds 'n'.\n    while (power << 1) <= n:\n        power <<= 1\n    return power\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/388", "solution": "```python\ndef highest_Power_of_2(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the highest power of 2 that is less than or equal to n.\n    Raises ValueError if n is less than or equal to 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    # Sets all bits to the right of the most significant bit.\n    n |= n >> 1\n    n |= n >> 2\n    n |= n >> 4\n    n |= n >> 8\n    n |= n >> 16\n    n |= n >> 32\n\n    # Returns the highest power of 2 less than or equal to the original n.\n    return (n + 1) >> 1\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/389", "solution": "```python\ndef find_lucas(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the n-th Lucas number.\n    The Lucas sequence is defined by L(0) = 2, L(1) = 1, and L(n) = L(n-1) + L(n-2) for n > 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 2\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    a, b = 2, 1  # L(0), L(1)\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        a, b = b, a + b\n    return b\n```"}
