{"task_id": "Mbpp/389", "solution": "```python\ndef find_lucas(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Nth Lucas number.\n\n    Args:\n        n: The index of the Lucas number to find. Must be a non-negative integer.\n\n    Returns:\n        The Nth Lucas number.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If n is not a non-negative integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 1\n    else:\n        a, b = 2, 1  # L(0) = 2, L(1) = 1\n        for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n            a, b = b, a + b\n        return b\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/390", "solution": "```python\nclass FormattingError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for errors during string formatting operations.\n    It encapsulates a message and the original exception.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, message: str, original_exception: Exception):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n        self.original_exception = original_exception\n\nfrom typing import Any\n\ndef add_string(data_list: list[Any], format_string: str) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Applies a given format string to all elements in a list, returning a new list.\n    Raises FormattingError if any element cannot be formatted.\"\"\"\n    formatted_results: list[str] = []\n    for i, element in enumerate(data_list):\n        try:\n            formatted_results.append(format_string.format(element))\n        except (ValueError, TypeError) as e:\n            raise FormattingError(\n                f\"Failed to format element at index {i} ('{element}') \"\n                f\"with format string '{format_string}'.\",\n                original_exception=e\n            ) from e\n    return formatted_results\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "```python\ndef set_left_most_unset_bit(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets the leftmost (most significant) unset bit in an integer.\n    Returns the integer with the leftmost unset bit set, or the original integer if no unset bit is found.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        # Negative numbers in two's complement typically have leading 1s.\n        return n\n    \n    if n == 0:\n        # For 0, the leftmost unset bit is at position 0, making it 1.\n        return 1\n\n    msb_pos = n.bit_length() - 1\n\n    for i in range(msb_pos, -1, -1):\n        if not (n & (1 << i)): # Checks if bit 'i' is 0.\n            return n | (1 << i) # Sets the identified unset bit.\n    \n    # If all bits up to msb_pos are set, extend the number by setting the next bit.\n    return n | (1 << (msb_pos + 1))\n```"}
