{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "```python\nfrom functools import lru_cache\n\n@lru_cache(maxsize=None)\ndef get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum sum for n recursively with memoization.\n    It follows f(n) = max( (f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n).\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        return 0\n\n    sum_of_parts = (\n        get_max_sum(n // 2) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 3) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 4) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 5)\n    )\n    return max(sum_of_parts, n)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/395", "solution": "```python\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom typing import Optional\n\ndef first_non_repeating_character(s: str) -> Optional[str]:\n    \"\"\"Finds the first non-repeated character in a string.\n    Returns None if no such character exists or the string is empty.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n    if not s:\n        return None\n\n    # Count character occurrences in the string.\n    char_counts = Counter(s)\n\n    # Iterate through the string to find the first character with a count of 1.\n    for char in s:\n        if char_counts[char] == 1:\n            return char\n    return None\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Dict\n\n# Module-level dictionary for memoization, storing previously computed f(n) values.\n_memo: Dict[int, int] = {}\n\ndef get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the maximum sum for a non-negative integer n using a recursive equation.\n    Memoization is used to store and retrieve previously computed results for efficiency.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    if n <= 1:\n        result = n\n    else:\n        # Recursively calculate sums for n/2, n/3, n/4, n/5 using integer division.\n        sum_of_parts = (\n            get_max_sum(n // 2) +\n            get_max_sum(n // 3) +\n            get_max_sum(n // 4) +\n            get_max_sum(n // 5)\n        )\n        # The result is the maximum of n itself or the sum of its parts.\n        result = max(sum_of_parts, n)\n\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result\n```"}
