{"task_id": "Mbpp/398", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_of_digits(numbers: list[int | float]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the sum of digits of each number in a given list and returns the total sum.\n    Raises TypeError if input is not a list or if any element is not a number.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(numbers, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list of numbers.\")\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for num in numbers:\n        if not isinstance(num, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(f\"List elements must be numbers, got {type(num).__name__}.\")\n\n        abs_num = abs(num) # Use absolute value to sum digits for negative numbers.\n        num_str = str(abs_num) # Convert number to string to iterate over its digits.\n\n        # For floats, convert to string and sum all numeric characters.\n        # The decimal point is ignored. Example: 3.5 -> \"3.5\" -> 3 + 5 = 8.\n        for digit_char in num_str:\n            if digit_char.isdigit():\n                total_sum += int(digit_char)\n    return total_sum\n```\n"}
