{"task_id": "Mbpp/300", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef count_binary_seq(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the count of all binary sequences of length 2n where the sum of the first n bits\n    is the same as the sum of the last n bits. It leverages the combinatorial identity C(2n, n).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Validate that n is a non-negative integer as per requirements.\n    # Raises ValueError if n is not an integer or is negative.\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(f\"n must be a non-negative integer, but got {n}\")\n    \n    # The count is given by the central binomial coefficient C(2n, n).\n    # This identity arises from summing C(n, k)^2 for k from 0 to n.\n    return math.comb(2 * n, n)\n```"}
