{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "```python\nclass ShellSortError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for errors in the Shell Sort implementation.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(self.message)\n\ndef shell_sort(arr: list) -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list in-place using the Shell Sort algorithm.\n    Raises ShellSortError if the input is not a list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(arr, list):\n        raise ShellSortError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return\n\n    # Start with a large gap and reduce it until 1.\n    # This uses a simple n // 2 gap sequence.\n    gap = n // 2\n    while gap > 0:\n        for i in range(gap, n):\n            temp = arr[i]\n            j = i\n            # Perform gapped insertion sort for the current gap.\n            while j >= gap and arr[j - gap] > temp:\n                arr[j] = arr[j - gap]\n                j -= gap\n            arr[j] = temp\n        gap //= 2\n```"}
