{"task_id": "Mbpp/429", "solution": "```python\nclass TupleValidationError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for validation errors related to tuple operations.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\ndef and_tuples(tuple1: tuple[int, ...], tuple2: tuple[int, ...]) -> tuple[int, ...]:\n    \"\"\"Performs an element-wise bitwise AND operation on two tuples of integers.\n    Returns a new tuple with the results, raising TupleValidationError for invalid inputs.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(tuple1, tuple) or not isinstance(tuple2, tuple):\n        raise TupleValidationError(\"Both inputs must be tuples.\")\n\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise TupleValidationError(\"Input tuples must have the same length.\")\n\n    results = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        e1 = tuple1[i]\n        e2 = tuple2[i]\n\n        if not isinstance(e1, int) or not isinstance(e2, int):\n            raise TupleValidationError(\"All elements in input tuples must be integers.\")\n\n        results.append(e1 & e2)\n\n    return tuple(results)\n```"}
