{"task_id": "Mbpp/457", "solution": "```python\nclass InvalidInputError(TypeError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input to the Find_Min utility.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n\ndef Find_Min(list_of_lists: list[list]) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies the sublist with the minimum length from a given list of lists.\n    Returns the first encountered sublist if multiple have the same minimum length.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(list_of_lists, list):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n\n    if not list_of_lists:\n        return []\n\n    min_length = float('inf')\n    result_sublist = []\n\n    for sublist in list_of_lists:\n        if not isinstance(sublist, list):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"All elements in the input list must be lists.\")\n\n        if len(sublist) < min_length:\n            min_length = len(sublist)\n            result_sublist = sublist\n    \n    return result_sublist\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/457", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Any, List, Optional\n\ndef Find_Min(list_of_lists: List[List[Any]]) -> Optional[List[Any]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the sublist with the minimum length from a list of lists.\n    Returns the first encountered shortest sublist or None if the input list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(list_of_lists, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n\n    if not list_of_lists:\n        return None\n\n    min_sublist: Optional[List[Any]] = None\n    min_length: int = float('inf') # type: ignore\n\n    for sublist in list_of_lists:\n        if not isinstance(sublist, list):\n            raise ValueError(\"All elements in the input list must be lists.\")\n        \n        if len(sublist) < min_length:\n            min_length = len(sublist)\n            min_sublist = sublist\n            # If an empty list is found, it's the shortest possible.\n            if min_length == 0:\n                break\n        \n    return min_sublist\n```"}
