{"task_id": "Mbpp/460", "solution": "```python\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input to the list extractor.\n    It provides a descriptive message explaining the reason for the invalid input.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n\ndef Extract(data: list[list]) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Extracts the first element from each sublist within the input data.\n    Raises InvalidInputError if 'data' or its elements are not valid lists.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(data, list):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input 'data' must be a list.\")\n\n    result = []\n    for i, sublist in enumerate(data):\n        if not isinstance(sublist, list):\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"Element at index {i} is not a list: {sublist}\")\n        if sublist:\n            result.append(sublist[0])\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/462", "solution": "```python\ndef combinations_list(input_list: list) -> list[list]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates all possible combinations (power set) from the input list,\n    following the order demonstrated in the user's example.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = [[]]\n\n    for item in input_list:\n        # Create new combinations by prepending the current item to all existing combinations.\n        new_combinations_from_item = []\n        for existing_combination in result:\n            new_combinations_from_item.append([item] + existing_combination)\n        \n        # Add these new combinations to the main result list.\n        result.extend(new_combinations_from_item)\n        \n    return result\n```"}
