{"task_id": "Mbpp/473", "solution": "```python\ndef tuple_intersection(list1: list[tuple], list2: list[tuple]) -> set[tuple]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the intersection of two lists of tuples, ignoring element order within tuples.\n    Returns a set of normalized tuples common to both input lists.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _normalize_tuple(tup: tuple) -> tuple:\n        \"\"\"\n        Normalizes a tuple by sorting its elements for a canonical representation.\n        Raises TypeError if the input is not a tuple.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(tup, tuple):\n            raise TypeError(f\"Expected a tuple, but got {type(tup)}\")\n        return tuple(sorted(tup))\n\n    if not isinstance(list1, list):\n        raise TypeError(f\"Expected list1 to be a list, but got {type(list1)}\")\n    if not isinstance(list2, list):\n        raise TypeError(f\"Expected list2 to be a list, but got {type(list2)}\")\n\n    normalized_set1 = set()\n    for tup in list1:\n        normalized_set1.add(_normalize_tuple(tup))\n\n    intersection_result = set()\n    for tup in list2:\n        normalized_tup = _normalize_tuple(tup)\n        if normalized_tup in normalized_set1:\n            intersection_result.add(normalized_tup)\n\n    return intersection_result\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/474", "solution": "```python\ndef replace_char(input_string: str, old_char: str, new_char: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Replaces all occurrences of old_char with new_char in input_string.\n    Raises TypeError for invalid input_string or ValueError for invalid old/new characters.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_string, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"input_string must be a string.\")\n    if not isinstance(old_char, str) or len(old_char) != 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"old_char must be a single character string.\")\n    if not isinstance(new_char, str) or len(new_char) != 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"new_char must be a single character string.\")\n\n    return input_string.replace(old_char, new_char)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/473", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Set, Any\n\ndef tuple_intersection(list1: List[Tuple[Any, ...]], list2: List[Tuple[Any, ...]]) -> Set[Tuple[Any, ...]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the intersection of elements in two given tuple lists, ignoring element order within tuples.\n    The result set contains original tuple representations from `list1` for matched items.\n    \"\"\"\n    normalized_to_original_map = {}\n    for t1 in list1:\n        # Convert tuple to frozenset for order-agnostic hashing.\n        normalized_to_original_map[frozenset(t1)] = t1\n\n    result_set: Set[Tuple[Any, ...]] = set()\n    for t2 in list2:\n        if frozenset(t2) in normalized_to_original_map:\n            result_set.add(normalized_to_original_map[frozenset(t2)])\n\n    return result_set\n```\n"}
