{"task_id": "Mbpp/562", "solution": "```python\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input data.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n\nfrom typing import Any, List\n\ndef Find_Max_Length(data: List[List[Any]]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum length among all sublists in the given data.\n    It validates the input before performing the calculation.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(data, list):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input 'data' must be a list.\")\n    \n    for i, item in enumerate(data):\n        if not isinstance(item, list):\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"Element at index {i} is not a list: {type(item)}\")\n\n    # If the input list of lists is empty, the max length is 0.\n    if not data:\n        return 0\n    \n    max_length = 0\n    # Iterate through each sublist to find and track the maximum length.\n    for sublist in data:\n        max_length = max(max_length, len(sublist))\n    \n    return max_length\n```"}
