{"task_id": "Mbpp/580", "solution": "```python\ndef extract_even(input_tuple: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"Recursively extracts even integers from a nested tuple, preserving its structure.\n    Non-integer and non-tuple elements are ignored, and empty nested tuples are excluded.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for item in input_tuple:\n        if isinstance(item, int):\n            if item % 2 == 0:\n                result.append(item)\n        elif isinstance(item, tuple):\n            # Recursively process nested tuples\n            nested_result = extract_even(item)\n            # Only append if the nested tuple is not empty after filtering\n            if nested_result:\n                result.append(nested_result)\n    return tuple(result)\n```"}
