{"task_id": "Mbpp/586", "solution": "```python\ndef split_Arr(arr: list, n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Splits a list at index n and moves the initial segment to the end.\n    Returns a new list with the reordered elements.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(arr, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'arr' must be a list.\")\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n    \n    if not (0 <= n <= len(arr)):\n        raise IndexError(f\"Index 'n' ({n}) is out of bounds for a list of length {len(arr)}.\")\n\n    first_part = arr[:n]\n    second_part = arr[n:]\n    return second_part + first_part\n```"}
