{"task_id": "Mbpp/588", "solution": "```python\ndef big_diff(numbers: list[int | float]) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the difference between the largest and smallest numbers in a list.\n    Handles various input validations and returns a non-negative difference.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(numbers, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n    if not all(isinstance(n, (int, float)) for n in numbers):\n        raise TypeError(\"All elements in the list must be numbers (int or float).\")\n    if not numbers:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list cannot be empty.\")\n\n    min_val = min(numbers)\n    max_val = max(numbers)\n    return max_val - min_val\n```"}
