{"task_id": "Mbpp/599", "solution": "```python\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input values.\n    It carries a descriptive message about the input error.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\ndef sum_average(n):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum and average of the first 'n' natural numbers.\n    Raises InvalidInputError if 'n' is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise InvalidInputError(f\"'n' must be an integer.\")\n    if n <= 0:\n        raise InvalidInputError(f\"'n' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    # Calculate sum using the formula: sum = n * (n + 1) / 2\n    sum_val = n * (n + 1) // 2\n\n    # Calculate average using the formula: average = sum / n\n    average_val = sum_val / n\n\n    return (sum_val, average_val)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/602", "solution": "```python\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input types.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n\nERROR_INVALID_INPUT_TYPE = \"Input must be a string.\"\n\ndef first_repeated_char(s: str) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first character that appears more than once in the given string.\n    Returns None if no character is repeated, or raises InvalidInputError for non-string input.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise InvalidInputError(ERROR_INVALID_INPUT_TYPE)\n\n    seen_chars = set()\n    for char in s:\n        if char in seen_chars:\n            return char\n        seen_chars.add(char)\n    return None\n```"}
