{"task_id": "Mbpp/597", "solution": "```python\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input to the find_kth function.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n\n\ndef find_kth(arr1: list[int], arr2: list[int], k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the k-th smallest element from two given sorted arrays.\n    Uses a recursive binary search approach to achieve O(log(min(N, M))) complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    n1, n2 = len(arr1), len(arr2)\n\n    # Validate k as per FR1 Error Handling.\n    if not (1 <= k <= n1 + n2):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\n            f\"k must be between 1 and {n1 + n2} (inclusive), but got {k}\"\n        )\n\n    def _get_kth_element_recursive_impl(a: list[int], b: list[int], current_k: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Recursive helper to find the k-th element using a binary search partition strategy.\n        It ensures valid partition indices and reduces the problem size logarithmically.\n        \"\"\"\n        len_a, len_b = len(a), len(b)\n\n        # Base cases: If one array is exhausted, the k-th element must be in the other.\n        if len_a == 0:\n            return b[current_k - 1]\n        if len_b == 0:\n            return a[current_k - 1]\n        # If k is 1, the smallest element is the minimum of the first elements.\n        if current_k == 1:\n            return min(a[0], b[0])\n\n        # Determine partition sizes for 'a' and 'b' aiming for roughly 'k/2' from each.\n        idx_a = min(current_k // 2, len_a)\n        idx_b = current_k - idx_a\n\n        # Adjust partition if `idx_b` overshoots `len_b` to ensure valid indexing.\n        if idx_b > len_b:\n            idx_b = len_b\n            idx_a = current_k - idx_b\n\n        # Compare elements at the chosen partitions to eliminate a portion of one array.\n        if a[idx_a - 1] <= b[idx_b - 1]:\n            # The k-th element is not in `a[:idx_a]`. Recurse on `a[idx_a:]`.\n            return _get_kth_element_recursive_impl(a[idx_a:], b, current_k - idx_a)\n        else:\n            # The k-th element is not in `b[:idx_b]`. Recurse on `b[idx_b:]`.\n            return _get_kth_element_recursive_impl(a, b[idx_b:], current_k - idx_b)\n\n    # Ensure arr1 (the first argument to the recursive helper) is the shorter array for optimization.\n    if n1 > n2:\n        return _get_kth_element_recursive_impl(arr2, arr1, k)\n    \n    return _get_kth_element_recursive_impl(arr1, arr2, k)\n```"}
