{"task_id": "Mbpp/620", "solution": "```python\ndef largest_subset(nums: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the size of the largest subset from a given list of integers\n    where every pair within the subset is divisible. Handles non-negative integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(nums, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n    \n    if not nums:\n        return 0\n\n    has_zero = False\n    positive_unique_nums = set() # Collect unique positive integers\n    for item in nums:\n        if not isinstance(item, int):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements in the list must be integers.\")\n        if item < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"All elements in the list must be non-negative integers.\")\n        if item == 0:\n            has_zero = True\n        else:\n            positive_unique_nums.add(item)\n\n    clean_nums = sorted(list(positive_unique_nums))\n\n    if not clean_nums: # Only zeros were present, or list was empty/only non-positives\n        return 1 if has_zero else 0\n\n    n = len(clean_nums)\n    dp = [1] * n # dp[i] stores the size of the largest divisible subset ending with clean_nums[i]\n\n    max_subset_size_positives = 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if clean_nums[i] % clean_nums[j] == 0:\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], dp[j] + 1)\n        max_subset_size_positives = max(max_subset_size_positives, dp[i])\n\n    # If 0 was present, it can form a subset [0] of size 1. It cannot be combined with positive numbers.\n    return max(1, max_subset_size_positives) if has_zero else max_subset_size_positives\n```"}
