{"task_id": "Mbpp/623", "solution": "```python\ndef nth_nums(numbers: list[float | int], n: int) -> list[float | int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the n-th power of each number in a list.\n    Raises TypeError for invalid input types.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(numbers, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'numbers' must be a list.\")\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n\n    results = []\n    for x in numbers:\n        if not isinstance(x, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(f\"All elements in 'numbers' must be numeric, but found type {type(x).__name__}.\")\n        results.append(x ** n)\n    return results\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/623", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\ndef nth_nums(numbers: List[Union[int, float]], n: int) -> List[Union[int, float]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the n-th power of each number in the input list.\n    Raises TypeError for invalid input types or non-numeric list elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(numbers, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'numbers' must be a list.\")\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n\n    for item in numbers:\n        if not isinstance(item, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(f\"List elements must be numeric, got {type(item).__name__}.\")\n\n    return [num ** n for num in numbers]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "```python\ndef get_median(list1: list[int], list2: list[int], n: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the median of two sorted lists of integers, each of size n, using an O(log n) approach.\"\"\"\n    # Validate inputs as per FR1, FR3, and error handling.\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Size 'n' cannot be negative.\")\n    if n == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Cannot find median of empty lists.\")\n    if len(list1) != n or len(list2) != n:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input lists must be of size n.\")\n\n    def find_kth_element(arr1, idx1, arr2, idx2, k):\n        \"\"\"Helper function to find the k-th smallest element (1-indexed) in two sorted arrays.\"\"\"\n        len1 = len(arr1) - idx1\n        len2 = len(arr2) - idx2\n\n        # Ensure arr1 is the shorter array (or equal length) to simplify recursive calls.\n        if len1 > len2:\n            return find_kth_element(arr2, idx2, arr1, idx1, k)\n\n        # Base cases for recursion.\n        if len1 == 0:  # If the first array is exhausted, return k-th from the second.\n            return arr2[idx2 + k - 1]\n        if k == 1:     # If k is 1, return the minimum of the first elements.\n            return min(arr1[idx1], arr2[idx2])\n\n        # Divide k into two parts for binary search comparison.\n        part1 = min(k // 2, len1)\n        part2 = k - part1\n\n        # Compare elements at the split points and recurse.\n        if arr1[idx1 + part1 - 1] < arr2[idx2 + part2 - 1]:\n            # Discard first 'part1' elements from arr1 and reduce k.\n            return find_kth_element(arr1, idx1 + part1, arr2, idx2, k - part1)\n        else:\n            # Discard first 'part2' elements from arr2 and reduce k.\n            return find_kth_element(arr1, idx1, arr2, idx2 + part2, k - part2)\n\n    # For 2*n elements, the median is the average of the n-th and (n+1)-th smallest elements (1-indexed).\n    median_val1 = find_kth_element(list1, 0, list2, 0, n)\n    median_val2 = find_kth_element(list1, 0, list2, 0, n + 1)\n\n    return (median_val1 + median_val2) / 2.0\n```"}
