{"task_id": "Mbpp/638", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input values.\n    It signals that an input parameter is not valid for the calculation.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n\ndef wind_chill(velocity: float, temperature: float) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the wind chill index based on wind velocity and temperature.\n    The result is rounded up to the next highest integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if velocity < 0:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Wind velocity cannot be negative.\")\n\n    # Wind Chill Index Formula (for Celsius and km/h):\n    # WCI = 13.12 + 0.6215 * T - 11.37 * V^0.16 + 0.3965 * T * V^0.16\n    \n    # If velocity is 0, the wind chill index is equal to the temperature.\n    if velocity == 0:\n        raw_wind_chill = temperature\n    else:\n        v_power_0_16 = math.pow(velocity, 0.16)\n        raw_wind_chill = (\n            13.12\n            + (0.6215 * temperature)\n            - (11.37 * v_power_0_16)\n            + (0.3965 * temperature * v_power_0_16)\n        )\n    \n    return math.ceil(raw_wind_chill)\n```"}
