{"task_id": "Mbpp/641", "solution": "```python\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input parameters.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n\ndef is_nonagonal(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth nonagonal number.\n    Raises InvalidInputError if n is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer.\")\n    \n    # Formula for the nth nonagonal number: n * (7n - 5) / 2\n    return (n * (7 * n - 5)) // 2\n```"}
