{"task_id": "Mbpp/638", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input values.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\ndef wind_chill(wind_velocity: float, temperature: float) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the wind chill index rounded to the next integer given the wind velocity\n    in km/h and a temperature in celsius.\n\n    Args:\n        wind_velocity: Wind speed in kilometers per hour (km/h).\n        temperature: Air temperature in Celsius (\u00b0C).\n\n    Returns:\n        The wind chill index as an integer, rounded up to the next whole number.\n\n    Raises:\n        InvalidInputError: If wind_velocity is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if wind_velocity < 0:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Wind velocity cannot be negative.\")\n\n    # Constants for the wind chill formula (Canadian model, km/h and Celsius)\n    # WCI = 13.12 + 0.6215 * T - 11.37 * V^0.16 + 0.3965 * T * V^0.16\n    CONSTANT_TERM = 13.12\n    BASE_TEMP_FACTOR = 0.6215\n    BASE_WIND_FACTOR = 11.37\n    TEMP_WIND_FACTOR = 0.3965\n    WIND_EXPONENT = 0.16\n\n    # For very low wind speeds (less than 4.8 km/h), the wind chill index is\n    # generally considered to be the air temperature itself, rounded up.\n    if wind_velocity < 4.8:\n        return math.ceil(temperature)\n\n    # Apply the standard Canadian wind chill formula.\n    wci_raw = (\n        CONSTANT_TERM\n        + (BASE_TEMP_FACTOR * temperature)\n        - (BASE_WIND_FACTOR * (wind_velocity**WIND_EXPONENT))\n        + (TEMP_WIND_FACTOR * temperature * (wind_velocity**WIND_EXPONENT))\n    )\n\n    # Round the result up to the next integer.\n    return math.ceil(wci_raw)\n\n```"}
