{"task_id": "Mbpp/644", "solution": "```python\ndef reverse_Array_Upto_K(arr: list, k: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Reverses the elements of an array from index 0 up to (but not including) index k in-place.\n    It returns the modified array, handling invalid input types and values with exceptions.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(arr, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'arr' must be a list.\")\n    if not isinstance(k, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'k' must be an integer.\")\n    if k < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'k' cannot be negative.\")\n\n    # Determine the actual end index for reversal, respecting array bounds and k.\n    end_index = min(k, len(arr))\n    \n    left = 0\n    right = end_index - 1\n\n    while left < right:\n        arr[left], arr[right] = arr[right], arr[left]\n        left += 1\n        right -= 1\n    \n    return arr\n```"}
