{"task_id": "Mbpp/726", "solution": "```python\ndef multiply_elements(input_tuple: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the product of adjacent elements in a tuple.\n    Returns an empty tuple if the input has fewer than two elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_tuple, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a tuple.\")\n    if len(input_tuple) < 2:\n        return ()\n    \n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(input_tuple) - 1):\n        result.append(input_tuple[i] * input_tuple[i+1])\n    return tuple(result)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/726", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Tuple, Union, Any\n\ndef multiply_elements(input_tuple: Tuple[Union[int, float], ...]) -> Tuple[Union[int, float], ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the product of adjacent elements in a tuple of numbers.\n    Returns an empty tuple if the input tuple has fewer than two elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_tuple, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a tuple.\")\n    for element in input_tuple:\n        if not isinstance(element, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements in the tuple must be numbers (int or float).\")\n\n    if len(input_tuple) < 2:\n        return ()\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(input_tuple) - 1):\n        result.append(input_tuple[i] * input_tuple[i+1])\n    return tuple(result)\n```"}
