{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "```python\ndef rotate_right(items: list, n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a list to the right by `n` positions.\n    Returns a new list without modifying the original.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(items, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'items' must be a list.\")\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n\n    if not items:\n        return []\n\n    items_length = len(items)\n    effective_n = n % items_length\n\n    # If effective_n is 0, no rotation is needed; return a copy.\n    if effective_n == 0:\n        return list(items)\n\n    # Perform rotation using slicing.\n    rotated_part = items[-effective_n:]\n    remaining_part = items[:-effective_n]\n    return rotated_part + remaining_part\n```"}
