{"task_id": "Mbpp/752", "solution": "```python\ndef jacobsthal_num(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth Jacobsthal number using an iterative approach.\n    Raises ValueError for negative input 'n'.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    # J(0) and J(1) are initialized as 'a' and 'b'.\n    a, b = 0, 1\n    # Iterate from J(2) up to J(n)\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        next_jacobsthal = b + 2 * a\n        a, b = b, next_jacobsthal\n    return b\n```"}
