{"task_id": "Mbpp/751", "solution": "```python\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input to min-heap checker.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str = \"Invalid input provided.\"):\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(self.message)\n\ndef check_min_heap(arr: list[int | float]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given array represents a min-heap.\n    Raises InvalidInputError if the input is not a list of numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(arr, list):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input must be a list of numbers.\")\n    for item in arr:\n        if not isinstance(item, (int, float)):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input must be a list of numbers.\")\n\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    # Iterate up to the last possible parent node.\n    for i in range(n // 2):\n        left_child_idx = 2 * i + 1\n        right_child_idx = 2 * i + 2\n\n        if left_child_idx < n and arr[i] > arr[left_child_idx]:\n            return False\n\n        if right_child_idx < n and arr[i] > arr[right_child_idx]:\n            return False\n            \n    return True\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/733", "solution": "```python\ndef find_first_occurrence(array: list[int], target: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the first occurrence of a given number in a sorted array.\n\n    Args:\n        array: A list of integers, sorted in non-decreasing order.\n        target: The integer to search for.\n\n    Returns:\n        The index of the first occurrence of the target, or -1 if not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not array:\n        return -1\n\n    low, high = 0, len(array) - 1\n    first_occurrence_index = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] == target:\n            first_occurrence_index = mid\n            high = mid - 1  # Try to find an earlier occurrence\n        elif array[mid] < target:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:  # array[mid] > target\n            high = mid - 1\n    return first_occurrence_index\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/753", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Any\n\ndef min_k(data_list: List[Tuple[Any, ...]], k_value: int) -> List[Tuple[Any, ...]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the 'k' records with the minimum values based on the second element of each tuple.\n    Raises ValueError for invalid k_value or IndexError for malformed tuples.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(k_value, int) or k_value < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"k_value must be a non-negative integer.\")\n    if k_value > len(data_list):\n        raise ValueError(\"k_value cannot be greater than the length of the data_list.\")\n\n    sorted_list = sorted(data_list, key=lambda x: x[1])\n    return sorted_list[:k_value]\n```"}
