{"task_id": "Mbpp/763", "solution": "```python\ndef find_min_diff(arr: tuple[int, ...], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum absolute difference between any two elements in `arr`.\n    Returns 0 if `arr` has less than two elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 2:\n        return 0\n\n    # Sort the array to easily find minimum difference between adjacent elements.\n    sorted_arr = sorted(arr)\n\n    min_diff = float('inf')\n\n    # Iterate through the sorted array to find the minimum difference.\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        current_diff = sorted_arr[i+1] - sorted_arr[i]\n        if current_diff < min_diff:\n            min_diff = current_diff\n    \n    return int(min_diff)\n```"}
