{"task_id": "Mbpp/765", "solution": "```python\ndef is_polite(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the nth polite number.\n\n    A polite number is any positive integer that is not a power of two.\n    The sequence of polite numbers starts with 3, 5, 6, 7, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15, ...\n\n    Args:\n        n: The positive integer representing the desired position in the sequence of polite numbers.\n\n    Returns:\n        The nth polite number.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If n is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    def is_power_of_two(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a positive integer is a power of two.\"\"\"\n        # Already validated num > 0 by outer function if num is current_number\n        return (num & (num - 1) == 0) and num != 0\n\n    polite_count = 0\n    current_number = 1\n    while True:\n        if not is_power_of_two(current_number):\n            polite_count += 1\n            if polite_count == n:\n                return current_number\n        current_number += 1\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/765", "solution": "```python\ndef is_power_of_two(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a positive integer is a power of two.\n    This function determines if only one bit is set in its binary representation.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(num, int) or num <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'num' must be a positive integer.\")\n    return (num & (num - 1)) == 0\n\ndef is_polite(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the nth polite number, which is any positive integer that is not a power of 2.\n    It iterates through numbers, counting those that are not powers of two.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    polite_count = 0\n    num = 0\n    while True:\n        num += 1\n        if not is_power_of_two(num):\n            polite_count += 1\n            if polite_count == n:\n                return num\n```"}
