{"task_id": "Mbpp/767", "solution": "```python\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef get_pairs_count(numbers: list[int], sum: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts pairs in `numbers` that sum to `sum`. Handles duplicates by counting combinations.\"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    freq_map = Counter(numbers)\n\n    for num in numbers:\n        complement = sum - num\n        \n        if complement in freq_map:\n            if num == complement:\n                # If num is its own complement, we need to choose 2 from its frequency.\n                count += (freq_map[num] * (freq_map[num] - 1)) // 2\n            else:\n                # If num and complement are different, multiply their frequencies.\n                count += freq_map[complement] * freq_map[num]\n            \n            # Mark numbers as processed to avoid double counting.\n            del freq_map[num]\n            if complement in freq_map:\n                del freq_map[complement]\n    return count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/770", "solution": "```python\ndef odd_num_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of the fourth power of the first n odd natural numbers.\n    Raises TypeError if n is not an integer, ValueError if n is negative.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        odd_number = 2 * i + 1\n        total_sum += odd_number ** 4\n    return total_sum\n```"}
