{"task_id": "Mbpp/767", "solution": "```python\nimport collections\nimport math\n\ndef get_pairs_count(numbers: list[int], sum: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts pairs in a list that sum to a target value.\n    Raises TypeError for invalid input types or non-integer list elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(numbers, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'numbers' must be a list.\")\n    if not all(isinstance(num, int) for num in numbers):\n        raise TypeError(\"All elements in 'numbers' must be integers.\")\n    if not isinstance(sum, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'sum' must be an integer.\")\n\n    if not numbers:\n        return 0\n\n    freq_map = collections.Counter(numbers)\n    pair_count = 0\n\n    for num in freq_map:\n        complement = sum - num\n\n        if complement in freq_map:\n            if num == complement:\n                # If num is its own complement, count combinations from its frequency.\n                count_of_num = freq_map[num]\n                if count_of_num >= 2:\n                    pair_count += math.comb(count_of_num, 2)\n            elif num < complement: # Ensures each unique pair (a,b) is counted only once.\n                # If num and complement are different, multiply their frequencies.\n                pair_count += freq_map[num] * freq_map[complement]\n\n    return pair_count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/769", "solution": "```python\ndef Diff(list1: list, list2: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the difference between two lists with a custom reordering rule.\n    The second element of the difference list is moved to the end if present.\n    \"\"\"\n    set_list2 = set(list2)\n    initial_diff = [item for item in list1 if item not in set_list2]\n\n    if len(initial_diff) >= 2:\n        second_element = initial_diff.pop(1)\n        initial_diff.append(second_element)\n\n    return initial_diff\n```\n"}
