{"task_id": "Mbpp/771", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Dict\n\ndef check_expression(expression: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Analyzes the input expression string to verify if all opening delimiters\n    have corresponding, correctly nested, and matched closing delimiters.\n    \"\"\"\n    stack: List[str] = []\n    \n    # Define recognized delimiters and their mapping.\n    opening_delimiters: str = \"([{\"\n    delimiter_map: Dict[str, str] = {\n        '(': ')',\n        '[': ']',\n        '{': '}'\n    }\n    closing_delimiters: str = \"\".join(delimiter_map.values())\n    \n    for char in expression:\n        if char in opening_delimiters:\n            stack.append(char)\n        elif char in closing_delimiters:\n            if not stack:\n                return False\n            \n            last_opening_delimiter = stack.pop()\n            if delimiter_map.get(last_opening_delimiter) != char:\n                return False\n    \n    return not stack\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/773", "solution": "```python\ndef occurance_substring(main_string: str, sub_string: str) -> tuple[str, int, int] | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first occurrence of a substring within a main string.\n    Returns a tuple (substring, start_index, end_index) if found, otherwise None.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not sub_string:\n        raise ValueError(\"Substring cannot be empty.\")\n\n    start_index = main_string.find(sub_string)\n\n    if start_index != -1:\n        end_index = start_index + len(sub_string)\n        return (sub_string, start_index, end_index)\n    else:\n        return None\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/773", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Optional, Tuple\n\ndef occurance_substring(main_string: str, sub_string: str) -> Optional[Tuple[str, int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first occurrence and position of a substring within a string.\n    Returns a tuple (substring, start_index, end_index) if found, otherwise None.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(main_string, str) or not isinstance(sub_string, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Both main_string and sub_string must be strings.\")\n\n    if not sub_string:\n        # An empty substring is found at the beginning of any string.\n        return (sub_string, 0, 0)\n\n    start_index = main_string.find(sub_string)\n\n    if start_index != -1:\n        end_index = start_index + len(sub_string)\n        return (sub_string, start_index, end_index)\n    else:\n        return None\n```"}
