{"task_id": "Mbpp/801", "solution": "```python\ndef test_three_equal(a: int, b: int, c: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of equal integers among three inputs.\"\"\"\n    if not all(isinstance(arg, int) for arg in [a, b, c]):\n        raise TypeError(\"All inputs must be integers.\")\n\n    if a == b and b == c:\n        return 3\n    elif a == b or b == c or a == c:\n        return 2\n    else:\n        return 0\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/800", "solution": "```python\ndef remove_all_spaces(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Removes common whitespace characters (space, tab, newline, etc.) from the input string.\n    Raises TypeError if the input is not a string.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_string, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n\n    result = input_string.replace(\" \", \"\")\n    result = result.replace(\"\\t\", \"\")\n    result = result.replace(\"\\n\", \"\")\n    result = result.replace(\"\\r\", \"\")\n    result = result.replace(\"\\f\", \"\")\n    result = result.replace(\"\\v\", \"\")\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/803", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef is_perfect_square(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if the given integer is a perfect square. Returns True if it is, False otherwise.\"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        return False\n    if number == 0:\n        return True\n\n    # Use integer square root for efficiency and to avoid floating-point precision issues.\n    sqrt_num = math.isqrt(number)\n    return sqrt_num * sqrt_num == number\n```"}
