{"task_id": "Mbpp/805", "solution": "```python\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\ndef _validate_input(list_of_lists: list) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Validates that the top-level input is a list and contains only lists.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(list_of_lists, list):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n    for i, sublist in enumerate(list_of_lists):\n        if not isinstance(sublist, list):\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"Element at index {i} is not a list.\")\n\ndef _validate_sublist_elements(sublist: list, sublist_index: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Validates that all elements within a given sublist are numeric.\"\"\"\n    for i, element in enumerate(sublist):\n        if not isinstance(element, (int, float)):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\n                f\"Element '{element}' at sublist index {sublist_index}, element index {i} is not numeric.\"\n            )\n\ndef max_sum_list(list_of_lists: list[list[int | float]]) -> list[int | float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies and returns the sublist from a collection of lists whose elements sum to the highest value.\n    Handles input validation and various edge cases, including empty lists and non-numeric elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_input(list_of_lists)\n\n    if not list_of_lists:\n        return []\n\n    max_sum = float('-inf')\n    max_sum_list_result = []\n\n    for i, sublist in enumerate(list_of_lists):\n        _validate_sublist_elements(sublist, i)\n        current_sum = sum(sublist)\n        if current_sum > max_sum:\n            max_sum = current_sum\n            max_sum_list_result = sublist\n    \n    return max_sum_list_result\n```"}
